<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates largely lower.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates largely lower.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were largely lower on Thursday, pulled down by the closure of the Central Bank's overnight borrowing facility, traders said.</p>
<p>Only the two- and six-month rates were steady.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks got caught with a lot of cash on hand,&quot; a foreign bank dealer said. This prodded banks to offer their money at the swap market and led to softer PHIBOR rates, he said.</p>
<p>The Central Bank said it closed its overnight borrowing facility because it had already squared off.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  MARCH 20		 MARCH 19</p>
<p>    1 W		8  5/8		  8  3/4</p>
<p>    2 W		8  5/8		  8 11/16</p>
<p>    1 M		8  3/4		  8 13/16</p>
<p>    2 M		8  7/8		  8  7/8</p>
<p>    3 M		8  7/8		  8 15/16</p>
<p>    6 M		9  1/8		  9  1/8</p>
<p>    12M		9  1/2		  9  9/16</p>
<p>    VAL		21-Mar		  20-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
